It's not a bug. Bazel treats '\\' as an escape character on all platforms.

Comment in `src/main/cpp/rc_file.cc`:
```c++
// This will treat "#" as a comment, and properly
// quote single and double quotes, and treat '\'
// as an escape character.
blaze_util::Tokenize(line, '#', &words);
```

The correct path seperator in the "rc" file is `\\`, so `user.bazelrc` in **Steps to reproduce the problem** should be modified:
```
startup --output_user_root="D:\\Users\\username\\_bazel_username"
```
